**A model answer.** `tests/practice-values.spec.ts`:

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import { fillRegistrationForm } from './registration-helpers';

test('the filled form keeps its values', async ({ page }) => {
  await fillRegistrationForm(page, 'katy@example.com');

  await expect(page.locator("input[type='email']")).toHaveValue('katy@example.com');
  await expect(page.getByPlaceholder('Last Name')).toHaveValue('Lovelace');
  await expect(page.locator('#Skills')).toHaveValue('Java');
  await expect(page.locator('h2')).toContainText('Regis');
});
```

Run it with `npx playwright test tests/practice-values.spec.ts --project=chromium`:

```output
Running 1 test using 1 worker
  1 passed (25.0s)
```

**What to check in your own answer.** The three fields use `toHaveValue`, because a field's contents are its value. The heading uses `toContainText`, because `Regis` is part of its text, not the whole of it. The test itself does no filling, because `fillRegistrationForm` does it. The time may be different on your computer, because the website is slow at times.

